<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 9: </span>Metric illustration on <span id="S14.F9.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">abalone</span>. <span id="S14.F9.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Top row:</span> context spectra. <span id="S14.F9.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Bottom row:</span> solid curves are <math id="S14.F9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> divided by <math id="S14.F9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>6</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6</annotation></semantics></math>; dashed curves are the actual downstream prediction error. We divide <math id="S14.F9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S14.F9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>6</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6</annotation></semantics></math> to fit it in the same plot.</figcaption>
