</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 8: </span>Number of classes, nodes, edges, and fractions (%) of train/validation sets.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S23.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="S23.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S23.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S23.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S23.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the <span id="S23.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">transductive setting</span>, the samples in all four sets are available at train time. The learner hides the labels of val samples for validation. Thus, <math id="S23.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is the size of the train set, while <math id="S23.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> is the size of all other three sets combined.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S23.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S23.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S23.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the <span id="S23.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">inductive setting</span>, samples in the test set are invisible at train time. The learner hides the entire val set (samples and labels) for validation. Thus, <math id="S23.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is the size of the train set, while <math id="S23.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> is the size of the other set.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S23.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S23.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Label propagation (Label-Prop) only works for the transductive setting, and is implemented as follows:
Let <math id="S23.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{W}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑾</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{W}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the adjacency matrix of the graph, such that <math id="S23.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{W}}[i,j]=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑾</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{W}}[i,j]=1</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="S23.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S23.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> are connected, and <math id="S23.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> otherwise.
Let <math id="S23.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{D}}</annotation></semantics></math> be a diagonal matrix such that <math id="S23.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{D}}[i,i]=\sum_{j}{\bm{W}}[i,j]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mi>𝑾</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{D}}[i,i]=\sum_{j}{\bm{W}}[i,j]</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="S23.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{S}}={\bm{D}}^{-\frac{1}{2}}{\bm{W}}{\bm{D}}^{-\frac{1}{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑫</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑾</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑫</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{S}}={\bm{D}}^{-\frac{1}{2}}{\bm{W}}{\bm{D}}^{-\frac{1}{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib170" title="" class="ltx_ref">170</a>]</cite>, Label-Prop solves</p>
<table id="S23.Ex77" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S23.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\left({\bm{I}}_{m+n}-\eta{\bm{S}}\right)}\hat{{\bm{y}}}=\tilde{{\bm{y}}},\quad\text{where }{\bm{y}}=[{\bm{y}},{\bm{0}}_{m}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑺</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>where </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\left({\bm{I}}_{m+n}-\eta{\bm{S}}\right)}\hat{{\bm{y}}}=\tilde{{\bm{y}}},\quad\text{where }{\bm{y}}=[{\bm{y}},{\bm{0}}_{m}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S23.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Then, <math id="S23.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{{\bm{y}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{{\bm{y}}}</annotation></semantics></math> contains the predicted labels for all <math id="S23.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m+n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m+n)</annotation></semantics></math> samples.
On the other hand, STKR works for both transductive and inductive settings. Its base kernel <math id="S23.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as</p>
<table id="S23.Ex78" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S23.Ex78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k(x,x^{\prime})=(m+n)\frac{W(x,x^{\prime})}{\sqrt{D(x)D(x^{\prime})}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k(x,x^{\prime})=(m+n)\frac{W(x,x^{\prime})}{\sqrt{D(x)D(x^{\prime})}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S23.p4.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S23.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W(x_{i},x_{j})={\bm{W}}[i,j]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝑾</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W(x_{i},x_{j})={\bm{W}}[i,j]</annotation></semantics></math>.
For the transductive setting, <math id="S23.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(x_{i})={\bm{D}}[i,i]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝑫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(x_{i})={\bm{D}}[i,i]</annotation></semantics></math>;
for the inductive setting, <math id="S23.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(x_{i})=\sum_{j\notin\text{ test nodes}}W(x_{i},x_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∉</mo><mtext> test nodes</mtext></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(x_{i})=\sum_{j\notin\text{ test nodes}}W(x_{i},x_{j})</annotation></semantics></math>, that is the sum is taken over only visible nodes.</p>
</div>
